+## Power Source item experience and the RoF2 slot display
+
+The November 3/4 release deployed the item-XP rules, compatible item metadata loaders and slot-21 display. See `docs/releases/power-source-xp-20261103/README.md` and `docs/releases/power-source-xp-display-20261103/README.md`. A complete ordinary or Hunt four-tier family trains from eligible pre-AA combat XP. Required/recommended levels and held-class eligibility apply. Normal/Base through the next three qualities costs 80/160/240 comparable-kill equivalents. A training item and its augments give no worn benefits. Ordinary Power Sources retain their original behavior.
+
+`common/item_xp_{policy,metadata,inventory,eligibility}.h` and `zone/advanced_loot_inventory.cpp` own the saved, item-ID-bound custom_data. Exact-row updates retain saved GUID, augments, charges, binding, grip and explicit dye. An uncertain write quarantines the session. Box and #zoneforge consume eligible inputs and their partial XP with the regular 3/4/4 recipes. Never restore player inventories to roll back training. Older loaders can lose multi-key metadata. For a rollback after training, use a metadata-compatible binary.
+
